				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0ac3aae3-b997-4700-90e8-d5dbeb09e2e0")
	)
	(text "The power circuit for each LED is a simple Low Side driver, implemented using an nMOS transistor.\n\nGATE RESISTOR DIMENSIONING\nThe Gate Resistor used to limit the current spikes required to the driving logic (in this case one of the output Parallel Ports of the Shift Register), \nbecause of the capacitive behaviour of the nMOS gate. This is probably not stricly necessary because of the Shift Register internal output protection, \nbut a more controlled an well inside the maximum absolute ratings behvaiour will be helpful to improve the lifetime and reliability of the circuit.  \nIn pratice, with the Rg = 1kOhm --> I_gate_MAX = 3.3v / 1000 = 3.3 mA --> well inside the 35mA maximum output current for 74HC595\n\nGATE PULL DOWN\nThis resistor is added with the goal of allowing the gate to dischharge (and so pull the MOS in OFF state) even when the 74HC595 output \ngoes into Hi-Z state (controlled by the \"*G\" shift reg input, and can be used to control ALL LEDs PWM at once, reducing the overall SPI throughput).\nIn general, in order to speed up the nMOS turning OFF I want a smaller resistor, but I have two contrasting aspects that require the opposite condition: \nHigh voltage on gate when nMOS ON (this is a problem because of voltage divider  with Rg) and Static Power consumption in ON condition (because of series to GND with Rg). \nTo compute it, I set the minumum allowed Voltage in ON condition to 3V, in order to leave a good margin to the nMOS worst case threshold voltage Vgs(th) = 1.5V, \nbasically trying to achive the best nMOS operating condition (lowest R_ds_ON)\nand then compute the resulting static power consumption and dynamic behavior.\n--> Voltage divider --> 3V = 3.3V * (Rgs / (Rgs + Rg)) --> Rgs = (Vgs * Rg) / (Vcc - Vgs) = 10 kOhm \n--> Static current --> Istatic = Vcc / (Rg + Rgs) = 0.3 mA\n--> Static power --> Pstatic = Vcc * Istatic = 0.99 mW\n R_DS_ON \n\nDYNAMIC BEHAVIOUR\n--> Ciss = 50 pF (datasheet value at specified test conditions)\n\n--> Turn-ON:\n    Ron = Rg || Rgs = 909 Ohm\n    Tau_on = Ron * Ciss = 45.5 ns\n    Vgs(t) = 3.0 * (1 - exp(-t / Tau_on))\n    Ton = -Tau_on * ln(1 - 2.75/3.0) = 113 ns\n\n--> Turn-OFF (74HC595 output in Hi-Z):\n    Roff = Rgs = 10 kOhm\n    Tau_off = Roff * Ciss = 500 ns\n    Vgs(t) = 3.0 * exp(-t / Tau_off)\n    Toff = Tau_off * ln(3.0/0.5) = 896 ns\n\nLED CURRENT LIMITING RESISTORS\n\nThe resistors are dimensioned for a target current of 20 mA, using the minimum LED forward voltage and neglecting the MOSFET voltage drop (worst-case current estimate). \nStandard E12 resistors with 5% tolerance are selected.\n\nGREEN LED - APT1608SGD3 - Vf_typ = 2.2 V (Vf_min not specified)\n--> R_min = (3.3 - 2.2) / 0.020 = 55 Ohm --> R = 56 Ohm (E12)\n--> I_est = 1.1 / 56 = 19.64 mA --> P_res = I² * R = 21.6 mW --> P_mos = I² * 5 = 1.93 mW\n\nYELLOW LED - LY Q976.01-Q1R2-36-1 - Vf_min = 1.6 V\n--> R_min = (3.3 - 1.6) / 0.020 = 85 Ohm --> R = 91 Ohm (E12)\n--> I_max_est = 1.7 / 91 = 18.68 mA --> P_res = I² * R = 31.8 mW --> P_mos = I² * 5 = 1.75 mW\n\nRED LED - LR Q976.01-P2R2-1-20-R18 - Vf_min = 1.6 V\n--> R_min = (3.3 - 1.6) / 0.020 = 85 Ohm --> R = 91 Ohm (E12)\n--> I_max_est = 1.7 / 91 = 18.68 mA --> P_res = I² * R = 31.8 mW --> P_mos = I² * 5 = 1.75 mW"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.748 192.024 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9fcf05b0-3f87-4047-ae42-314aad68a40a")
	)
	(text "In order to reduce the number of MicroController pins needed to control all the LEDs on the HumanSide Master board,\nsome shift register are used\n\nThere is no need for nCS for the serial interface which is controlled by SPI, because\nthe firmware can guarantee either way the possibiity of the LED circuit to share\nits SPI with other circuits. \nThis is because the LED will always have shift register working (even when SPI is \ncommunicating with other devices), but the storageReg will only be updated after the SPI\ncommunicated with this device!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 28.448 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "afebaa08-ce8b-4434-8155-f1750e0c69be")
	)
	(text "Speedometer LED Strip"
